eline and evaluate error.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to identify reasons your forecast may fail in production.", "exercise": "Create and evaluate a baseline forecast.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 39, "week": 8, "level": "Pro", "title": "Governance, Privacy, Versioning & Documentation", "tool": "Data Governance", "concepts": "Data ownership, access, reproducibility, change logs and responsible handling.", "objectives": ["Create data dictionary", "Define owners", "Document changes", "Protect sensitive data"], "practical": "Design governance controls for a reporting system and create a change log.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to review the governance plan for missing operational risks; never paste sensitive real data.", "exercise": "Create a governance and auditability pack.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 40, "week": 8, "level": "Pro", "title": "Pro Capstone", "tool": "Python + BI + QA", "concepts": "Automated multi-source analysis with reproducible cleaning, QA, dashboard-ready outputs and documentation.", "objectives": ["Automate pipeline", "Validate outputs", "Create executive outputs", "Document assumptions"], "practical": "Build a repeatable analysis package from multiple raw files.", "ai_use": "Use AI as a code reviewer and skeptical analyst; retain human ownership of all conclusions.", "exercise": "Pro capstone: automated analytical pipeline.", "capstone": true}, {"day": 41, "week": 9, "level": "Expert", "title": "Analytical Problem Framing", "tool": "Analytical Thinking", "concepts": "From vague stakeholder request to decision, metric, population, grain, constraints and success criteria.", "objectives": ["Clarify the decision", "Define analytical unit", "Identify required evidence", "List assumptions"], "practical": "Turn three vague management questions into precise analysis plans.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to play a difficult stakeholder and challenge missing assumptions.", "exercise": "Write an analysis specification.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 42, "week": 9, "level": "Expert", "title": "Multi-Source Architecture & Lineage", "tool": "Data Architecture", "concepts": "Source, staging, model, semantic/report and QA layers with lineage.", "objectives": ["Design layers", "Document lineage", "Define refresh dependencies", "Plan exception handling"], "practical": "Design an architecture for five sources with owners and refresh rules.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to identify single points of failure in your architecture.", "exercise": "Create a data-flow and lineage design.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 43, "week": 9, "level": "Expert", "title": "Metric Layer & Semantic Consistency", "tool": "Analytics Engineering", "concepts": "Single definitions for KPIs, dimensions, time logic and business rules.", "objectives": ["Create metric dictionary", "Centralize rules", "Prevent conflicting definitions"], "practical": "Design a metric layer for a program with monthly, quarterly and annual reporting.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to find ambiguous KPI definitions and propose questions, not definitions.", "exercise": "Create a governed KPI/metric dictionary.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 44, "week": 9, "level": "Expert", "title": "Causal Reasoning & Decision Risk", "tool": "Statistics / Reasoning", "concepts": "Confounding, selection bias, causality vs correlation and decision uncertainty.", "objectives": ["Identify confounders", "Separate association from effect", "Communicate uncertainty"], "practical": "Review a case where performance improved and assess whether the intervention caused it.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to generate competing causal explanations and evidence needed to distinguish them.", "exercise": "Write a causal reasoning memo.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 45, "week": 9, "level": "Expert", "title": "Executive Communication & Analytical Narrative", "tool": "Communication", "concepts": "What executives need: decision, evidence, risk, recommendation and next action.", "objectives": ["Write an executive summary", "Prioritize findings", "Quantify uncertainty", "Recommend action"], "practical": "Convert a technical analysis into a one-page executive brief.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to critique clarity for a non-technical executive; do not let it change facts.", "exercise": "Produce an executive analytical brief.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 46, "week": 10, "level": "Expert", "title": "Model QA, Audit & Reconciliation", "tool": "QA / Audit", "concepts": "Control totals, regression checks, source-to-report tracing and test design.", "objectives": ["Design test suite", "Trace KPIs", "Detect regression", "Document evidence"], "practical": "Audit a supplied model and create a structured test matrix.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to generate adversarial test cases after you define the business rules.", "exercise": "Create a model QA and audit report.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 47, "week": 10, "level": "Expert", "title": "AI-Assisted Analytics Workflow", "tool": "AI + Analytics", "concepts": "Using AI for explanation, debugging, hypothesis generation, critique and documentation without surrendering verification.", "objectives": ["Choose appropriate AI role", "Protect sensitive data", "Verify AI claims", "Document AI-assisted work"], "practical": "Run a controlled AI-assisted analysis using a verification log: prompt, AI claim, evidence checked, final decision.", "ai_use": "Use AI as tutor/reviewer/adversary; never treat its output as a source of truth.", "exercise": "Create an AI-assisted analysis verification log.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 48, "week": 10, "level": "Expert", "title": "Live Change Request & Regression Testing", "tool": "Integrated Analytics", "concepts": "Changing a business rule safely across formulas, SQL, measures or code.", "objectives": ["Assess impact", "Centralize change", "Regression test", "Communicate effect"], "practical": "Apply a late KPI-rule change and prove unrelated outputs did not change.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to propose regression tests, then independently judge whether they are sufficient.", "exercise": "Implement and validate a change request.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 49, "week": 10, "level": "Expert", "title": "Stakeholder Defense & Technical Review", "tool": "Communication / QA", "concepts": "Defending methods, assumptions and findings under questioning.", "objectives": ["Explain methodology", "Respond to challenges", "Admit limitations", "Trace evidence"], "practical": "Prepare a 10-minute walkthrough and answer an assessor's technical and management questions.", "ai_use": "Ask AI to conduct a hostile-but-fair mock defense and score your responses.", "exercise": "Complete an oral defense rehearsal.", "capstone": false}, {"day": 50, "week": 10, "level": "Expert", "title": "Final Expert Capstone", "tool": "Integrated Data Analysis", "concepts": "End-to-end expert system: problem framing, multi-source data, cleaning, SQL/Python/BI, QA, AI verification, governance and executive communication.", "objectives": ["Build a complete analytical system", "Defend every KPI", "Automate repeatab